# Vibe-Coding Prompt Pack — MLR RuleOps Demo App

**Scope:** fully generic. No customer names, no real-world product or therapy-area branding. Products are `Product A / B / C / X`; therapy areas are generic (Cardiovascular, Respiratory, Oncology, Immunology, Infectious Diseases); all people are fictional.

**How to use:**
1. Run **Section 1** (Prompts D1–D5) to generate the synthetic dataset.
2. Paste **Section 2 · Prompt 1** to build the app.
3. Use **Prompts 2–6** to fix the failures these tools reliably produce.

---

# SECTION 1 — Synthetic data generation prompts

Run these first, in order. Each outputs a JSON file the app will consume. Use any LLM (AI Studio, ChatGPT, Claude) — these are data-generation prompts, not build prompts.

## Prompt D1 — MLR rules catalog

````
Generate a synthetic MLR (Medical/Legal/Regulatory) rules catalog as a JSON array of ~30 rules.
This is fake demo data for a software prototype. Do NOT use any real company, product, or brand
names. Use generic placeholders only.

DIMENSIONS
- product: "Product A", "Product B", "Product C", "Product X", or "ALL"
- therapyArea: Cardiovascular | Respiratory | Oncology | Immunology | Infectious Diseases | ALL
- market: Global, US, UK, DE, FR, JP, BR, CA, LATAM (+ language code e.g. en-US, de-DE, ja-JP)
- materialType: Promotional (HCP) | Promotional (Patient/DTC) | Scientific/Publication | ALL

RULE HIERARCHY — produce a realistic spread across all five layers:
- Universal (global, applies to everything) — about 3 rules
- Market-Specific (one market, all products) — about 7 rules
- Brand-Specific (one product, all markets) — about 6 rules
- Market-Brand-Specific (one market + one product; most granular) — about 9 rules
- Scientific-Accuracy (citation/statistics integrity) — about 4 rules
Plus 1 rule with status "Deprecated" representing the PRIOR version of a Market-Brand rule,
so a rollback can be demonstrated.

EACH RULE OBJECT:
{
  "ruleId": "e.g. MB-US-PRODA-CV-014",
  "layer": "Universal|Market-Specific|Brand-Specific|Market-Brand-Specific|Scientific-Accuracy",
  "market": "...", "language": "...", "product": "...", "therapyArea": "...",
  "materialType": "...",
  "ruleClass": "text-string" or "business-logic",
  "riskTier": "Low|Medium|High|Critical",
  "status": "Active" or "Deprecated",
  "version": "e.g. 5.2",
  "lastUpdated": "YYYY-MM-DD",
  "dependencies": ["ruleId", ...],
  "description": "one line, prefixed [ILLUSTRATIVE]",
  "content": "the actual text string, or null for logic rules",
  "trigger": "pseudo-code boolean, or null for text rules,
              e.g. IF market=='JP' AND materialType LIKE 'Promotional%' THEN route_to('JP-RA-Reviewer')",
  "restrictedTerms": ["...", ...]
}

REQUIREMENTS
- Mix text-string rules (disclaimers, PI hyperlinks, local contact details, adverse-event
  statements) and business-logic rules (routing, dual-review requirements, blocking).
- Include multilingual content for DE, FR, BR, JP rules.
- Include restricted-term lists (e.g. "cure", "100% safe", "best-in-class", "side-effect-free").
- Use placeholder URLs on example.com and fake registration numbers.
- Clinical/efficacy values must be placeholders like "XX.X" — never invent real-looking figures.
- Mark all content with [SYNTHETIC] or [ILLUSTRATIVE] so it can never be mistaken for real
  regulatory text.

DEMO-CRITICAL: include a rule with ruleId "MB-US-PRODA-CV-014" — a US Product A cardiovascular
promotional disclaimer whose content cites "(Smith et al., 2020, CV-OUTCOMES)". Also create
near-miss distractors: a Market-level US cardiovascular rule and a Brand-level global Product A
rule, so a disambiguation demo has realistic competing candidates.

Output valid JSON only.
````

## Prompt D2 — Mock tickets

````
Generate ~16 synthetic rule-change tickets as a JSON array, for a demo of AI-assisted MLR rule
updates. Generic placeholders only — no real company, product or person names.

EACH TICKET:
{
  "ticketId": "TKT-1001",
  "source": "ServiceNow" | "Jira",
  "submittedBy": "role-style fictional name, e.g. 'US Content Owner (M. Alvarez)'",
  "priority": "Low|Medium|High",
  "requestText": "plain-English request as a non-technical business user would write it",
  "category": "Text String Update" | "Business Logic Change" | "Rollback Request" | "Ambiguous / Incomplete",
  "expectedTargetRule": "ruleId, or 'AMBIGUOUS: ruleA vs ruleB' or 'NONE - insufficient info'",
  "matchConfidence": 0.22 to 0.96,
  "riskTier": "Low|Medium|High|Critical|Unknown",
  "autonomyTier": "Assisted|Supervised|Escalated",
  "hitlGate": "Gate1-IntentConfirm | Gate2-RuleMatch | Gate3-SingleApproval | Gate3-DualApproval | Gate3-Block",
  "notes": "what this ticket demonstrates in the demo"
}

MUST COVER THESE SCENARIOS (one ticket each, minimum):
1. GOLDEN PATH (TKT-1001): "Update the US cardiovascular disclaimer for Product A to include the
   new 2026 clinical trial citation and remove reference to the 2020 study." → clean 96% match on
   MB-US-PRODA-CV-014 → Low risk → single approval.
2. DISAMBIGUATION: request names the product but NOT the market, so 3 rules across different
   layers match → confidence ~62% → Gate2.
3. BUSINESS-LOGIC / CRITICAL: "if Product X is mentioned in Japan promotional material, require
   both RA and Scientific reviewer sign-off" → Critical → dual approval + RMCB reference.
4. GUARDRAIL BLOCK: asks to soften or weaken an approved safety warning → refused, escalated.
5. RESTRICTED TERM: asks to add a prohibited claim phrase as approved language → blocked.
6. ROLLBACK: asks to restore the previous version of a rule.
7. VERY LOW CONFIDENCE: vague ticket like "Please fix the disclaimer, it's wrong." → ~22% →
   Gate1 clarifying questions.
8. MULTILINGUAL: at least 3 tickets written in German, Portuguese and French.
9. MARKET-WIDE BLAST RADIUS: a PI hyperlink change affecting all products in one market.

Output valid JSON only.
````

## Prompt D3 — Content corpus (regression test set)

````
Generate ~15 synthetic content assets as a JSON array. These represent previously-reviewed
promotional/scientific materials that get re-scored whenever an MLR rule changes — the
regression test set. Generic placeholders only.

EACH ASSET:
{
  "contentId": "CNT-001",
  "market": "US|DE|JP|BR|UK|FR|LATAM",
  "product": "Product A|B|C|X",
  "therapyArea": "...",
  "materialType": "...",
  "bodyExcerpt": "one short line of the asset's text",
  "currentResult": "PASS" | "FAIL",
  "governingRules": ["ruleId", ...],
  "failReason": "why it fails, or null"
}

DEMO-CRITICAL REQUIREMENT:
Include exactly one asset (CNT-003) that currently FAILS *because* it references a 2026 citation
that is not yet present in the active rule. After the golden-path ticket is applied, this asset
must flip to PASS. Set its failReason to:
"References 2026 citation not yet in active rule (expected to PASS after TKT-1001)."

Also include:
- Several stable PASS assets that must remain unchanged (proving no collateral damage).
- 2-3 assets failing for UNRELATED reasons (restricted term, superlative claim, unverified
  statistic) that must stay FAIL — proving the change is surgical.
- At least one asset in a different market (DE) governed by a different rule, to prove the
  change did not leak across markets.

Output valid JSON only.
````

